  << /ActualText ( The Standard Countdown Algorithm\n\n\n1\056 Start  \n2\056 Accept the total countdown duration in seconds from the user\056\n3\056 Initiate a loop that runs as long as remaining seconds \076 0\056 \n4\056 In each iteration of the loop\072 \na\056 Divide total seconds by 60 to calculate total minutes and remaining seconds\056 \nb\056 Format the output to a 2\055digit digital clock structure \050MM\072SS\051\056 \nc\056 Print the formatted string using a carriage return \047\134r\047 to overwrite the line\056 \nd\056 Halt program execution for 1 second\056 \ne\056 Subtract 1 from the remaining seconds counter\056 \n5\056 Exit loop when remaining seconds hit 0\056\n 6\056 Display a termination message \050e\056g\056\054 \042Time\047s up\041\042\051\056\n 7\056 End)
